// The four entries a rotation touches.
//
// Every axis rotation is the same 2x2 block [c, -s; s, c] dropped into four
// slots of the identity; only which four slots differ. So there is one function
// with the slots as parameters, and the three axis builders are the three slot
// quadruples -- which is also what keeps them three legal functions rather than
// one function copied three times (bodies identical up to renaming are a compile
// error; distinct literals are what distinguish them).
//
// deg is millidegrees and fx_sin/fx_cos answer x1000, which is exactly the scale
// a matrix entry wants, so nothing is converted here.

m4_rot4(int[] mat, int i, int j, int k, int p, int deg) {
  int co = fx_cos(deg);
  int si = fx_sin(deg);
  m4_rot4_b(mat, i, j, k, p, co, si);
} return void;
